WEBVTT

00:02.100 --> 00:07.070
Mother, I found out that Able had a wife and son that he was separated from.

00:07.070 --> 00:10.940
To think that, despite still loving them dearly, he believes they'll be happier if he stays away...

00:12.450 --> 00:16.820
Right now, I'm on my way to Egypt following a clue from your diary.

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
NAAJA

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
Nadja,

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
With your eyes

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
Nadja,

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
NAAJA

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
What do you see?

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
Nani ga mieru

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Shining in the far distance,

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
The door to the future,

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
Mirai no tobira

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
That's what I'm searching for

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
Sagashite iru

00:43.560 --> 00:50.780
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
Minna egao de aetara

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
It could be so much more fun

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
I can't see the end of the journey

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
Tabi no owari wa mienai

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
God is the only one who could possibly know

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
I will go waving

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
Te wo furinagara

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
But I won't look back

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
Ushiro mukanai

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Until the day my dream comes true

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
Nadja, Your smile

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
Nadja, gives me courage

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Under the blue sky,

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Aoi sora no shita de

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
I will find the place

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
Ashita no yukue

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
where my future lies

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
Mitsukeru kara

01:55.050 --> 01:59.050
Granada, Spain
Gonzales Mansion

02:09.460 --> 02:13.710
﻿Even if I remain at a place like this, my prince won't come to escort me away.

02:13.710 --> 02:16.880
It's no good to stay here...

02:17.200 --> 02:18.070
Ow!

02:23.970 --> 02:25.310
﻿Rosemary!

02:26.680 --> 02:30.020
﻿There's someone here who says he wants to see you.

02:31.610 --> 02:32.770
﻿A guest...?

02:33.610 --> 02:35.070
﻿For me?

02:52.210 --> 02:54.290
﻿Are you Ms. Rosemary?

02:54.820 --> 02:55.650
Yes...

02:56.670 --> 02:59.050
﻿Umm... what can I help you with?

02:59.050 --> 03:04.800
﻿You... are a friend of a Ms. Nadja Applefield, correct?

03:04.800 --> 03:05.720
Yes.

03:05.720 --> 03:11.190
﻿We heard from Ms. Appleton of the Applefield Orphanage that you recently met with her.

03:12.900 --> 03:14.230
﻿Applefield...

03:15.570 --> 03:21.530
﻿So we were possibly thinking that you might know of Ms. Nadja's current whereabouts...

03:21.990 --> 03:22.820
﻿Not really.

03:24.120 --> 03:29.950
﻿All I know is that Nadja is currently with a group of traveling entertainers called the Dandelion Troupe.

03:29.960 --> 03:31.750
﻿Where she is now is anyone's guess.

03:31.750 --> 03:34.210
﻿A group of traveling entertainers, huh?

03:34.210 --> 03:36.670
﻿She's turning out to be pretty hard to catch...

03:36.670 --> 03:40.300
﻿But now that we know this, it shouldn't be too hard.

03:41.840 --> 03:44.720
﻿Why are you looking for Nadja?

03:45.180 --> 03:49.430
﻿Oh. we re just working as the clientele for a certain aristocrat.

03:50.230 --> 03:51.230
﻿An aristocrat?

03:52.100 --> 03:56.400
﻿What kind of relation does Nadja have to an aristocrat?

03:56.980 --> 04:00.860
﻿It couldn't be that Nadja's actually some daughter of a noble or something like that, right?

04:00.860 --> 04:02.150
﻿You're certainly a bright one!

04:02.150 --> 04:03.450
﻿What?!

04:05.160 --> 04:09.370
﻿No way! Nadja's the daughter of a noble?!

04:09.370 --> 04:12.000
﻿Don't go blabbing everything out!

04:12.000 --> 04:12.500
Yes...

04:12.500 --> 04:13.410
﻿Let's go.

04:14.170 --> 04:15.710
﻿Wait.

04:19.500 --> 04:23.720
I ﻿can be of some help to you gentlemen.

04:31.160 --> 04:36.170
The End of the Nile
The Secret of the Ring

04:40.530 --> 04:43.570
﻿"I met up with Professor Edward Harrison today after not seeing him for some time,

04:43.570 --> 04:45.990
﻿and danced a waltz with him tonight."

04:45.990 --> 04:49.410
﻿"It's been three years since I first met him in Egypt."

04:49.410 --> 04:52.870
﻿"The professor told me he was going to depart for Egypt again tomorrow."

04:52.870 --> 04:55.500
﻿"He told me that he was prepared to die there,

04:55.500 --> 04:58.830
﻿determined to spend his life trying to solve a riddle of some ruins he's in the middle of excavating."

04:58.840 --> 05:01.420
﻿"I wish him nothing but safety in his travels."

05:02.130 --> 05:04.050
﻿Professor Edward Harrison...

05:07.260 --> 05:08.970
﻿I wonder if I'll be able to meet him...

05:08.970 --> 05:11.140
﻿Well, Egypt is quite vast...

05:11.140 --> 05:15.060
﻿It'll be fine! We'll definitely find him for you!

05:15.060 --> 05:16.520
﻿That's right! Right?

05:17.480 --> 05:19.610
﻿After all, we have already come this far.

05:19.610 --> 05:21.650
﻿Yeah, yeah.

05:23.780 --> 05:26.200
﻿Everyone...! Thank you!

05:26.200 --> 05:27.950
﻿Hey! Take a look out here!

05:29.570 --> 05:30.280
﻿Over there.

05:32.580 --> 05:34.830
﻿Ah! It's a pyramid!

05:34.830 --> 05:37.120
﻿It's like building blocks!

05:39.000 --> 05:43.920
﻿Mother, right now, I might be looking at the same scenery you did when you were here so long ago.

05:45.760 --> 05:49.220
Assalamu alaikum, Egypt!

05:50.720 --> 05:54.470
﻿So, why don't we first of all, try heading over to the pyramid!

05:54.850 --> 05:56.640
﻿Yeah!

06:08.820 --> 06:10.610
﻿Hot! Hot! Hot hot hot!

06:10.620 --> 06:12.450
﻿What is with this heat?

06:12.870 --> 06:13.990
﻿It's so bright!

06:13.990 --> 06:16.160
﻿My entire body's getting all frizzy!

06:17.080 --> 06:20.370
﻿With this sun, tanning isn't the only thing that would happen to your body.

06:20.790 --> 06:22.630
﻿Excuse me!

06:22.630 --> 06:25.090
﻿Do any-of you know a person by the name of...

06:25.090 --> 06:27.050
﻿Edward Harrison?

06:31.260 --> 06:32.720
﻿So it's no good here...

06:33.220 --> 06:35.430
﻿But this is still just the first site!

06:35.430 --> 06:37.270
﻿No buried treasure, huh...

06:38.480 --> 06:40.640
﻿Hey! Let's head off to the next excavation site. The next one!

06:41.150 --> 06:43.150
﻿Yeah!

06:47.110 --> 06:48.360
﻿Excuse me!

06:49.280 --> 06:50.950
﻿Umm... do you know of...

06:52.700 --> 06:56.540
﻿Do any of you know of a Professor Edward Harrison?!

06:57.750 --> 06:59.620
﻿So no one here knows either...

07:00.250 --> 07:02.080
﻿This is still just the second one!

07:02.080 --> 07:03.790
﻿Onto the next one! The next one!

07:03.790 --> 07:05.290
﻿Yeah!

07:07.800 --> 07:12.470
﻿It looks like there haven't been any people here for some time...

07:16.680 --> 07:19.520
﻿But, this is still only the third excavation site.

07:19.520 --> 07:21.310
﻿Okay, let's move onto the next one then! The next one!

07:21.310 --> 07:22.350
﻿Yeah!

07:22.350 --> 07:23.400
﻿Yeah...

07:23.400 --> 07:24.020
﻿Yeah...

07:38.620 --> 07:40.660
﻿Let's hurry and dig out the car and move onto the next site!

07:40.660 --> 07:42.210
﻿Yeah...

08:11.110 --> 08:14.950
﻿Come on Nadja... you can't sleep here...

08:14.950 --> 08:16.620
﻿Nadja!

08:16.620 --> 08:17.780
﻿Mother...

08:36.760 --> 08:39.180
﻿But... this is still only the eighteenth site..

08:43.310 --> 08:44.810
﻿Thomas!

08:44.810 --> 08:46.730
﻿Hey, Thomas!

08:55.280 --> 08:57.990
﻿No!! What's with this suntan?!

08:57.990 --> 09:00.200
﻿And not only that, my skin's all crackled!

09:00.200 --> 09:03.700
﻿This is why I hate hot places! Geez!

09:04.710 --> 09:07.620
﻿G-Granny, p-p-please gently now!

09:07.630 --> 09:12.130
﻿What are you saying? You're making a whole hullabaloo over some small blisters like this?

09:12.130 --> 09:13.670
﻿Here! Here, here!

09:13.670 --> 09:16.130
﻿Ow! Ow ow! Ow ow ow!

09:16.550 --> 09:17.550
﻿Does this feel good?

09:17.550 --> 09:18.240
Yeah.

09:19.970 --> 09:21.760
﻿Nadja, are you going back out?

09:21.770 --> 09:26.390
﻿Yeah, I heard there were lots of other excavation sites around this village.

09:26.390 --> 09:28.020
﻿So I'm going to take a look around.

09:28.020 --> 09:29.610
The rest of you, rest up well.

09:29.610 --> 09:31.320
﻿Wait, Nadja.

09:31.320 --> 09:33.360
﻿I'll go with you.

09:34.570 --> 09:39.030
﻿But really, Egypt sure is big... there's a ton of sites everywhere.

09:39.030 --> 09:43.240
﻿Yeah. I didn't think it would be this tough.

09:43.240 --> 09:48.000
﻿Oh, that reminds me. Christian also must be working hard at some site somewhere.

09:48.000 --> 09:49.040
﻿You mean that Mummy Professor?

09:50.460 --> 09:53.670
﻿I see... I guess he came to Egypt too, didn't he?

09:53.670 --> 09:56.590
﻿Wouldn't it be funny if we just happened to run into each other somewhere?

09:56.590 --> 09:57.880
﻿Well, I guess that wouldn't happen.

09:58.340 --> 10:01.010
﻿Well I don't really want to see him again, so...

10:01.430 --> 10:02.850
﻿Ah, it's nothing!

10:06.520 --> 10:07.680
Excuse me!

10:10.630 --> 10:11.500
Merci.

10:13.360 --> 10:14.440
﻿How was it?

10:14.440 --> 10:16.650
﻿It looks like he didn't know who I was talking about either.

10:16.650 --> 10:20.070
﻿And it also seems like those guys over there are all a part of an excavation team from France.

10:20.070 --> 10:24.450
﻿From the sound of "Edward Harrison, it's more like the name of an Englishman or an American, right?

10:24.450 --> 10:27.160
﻿At any rate, let's try asking anyone we might run into.

10:27.160 --> 10:27.830
﻿Yeah.

10:31.500 --> 10:32.880
﻿Danke!

10:33.920 --> 10:35.590
Grazie!

10:36.130 --> 10:38.670
﻿German and Italian teams, huh?

10:38.680 --> 10:42.220
﻿Starting around the 18th century, amongst the citizens of Europe,

10:42.220 --> 10:44.930
﻿ruin excavations became incredibly popular

10:44.930 --> 10:50.060
﻿and many people from many countries began to visit Egypt.

10:50.060 --> 10:53.110
﻿This is the last hotel in the village.

10:53.110 --> 10:54.000
Yeah.

10:54.570 --> 10:59.440
﻿Let's see... yes, one group like that is staying here. An excavation team from England.

10:59.990 --> 11:01.140
﻿England?!

11:01.140 --> 11:02.010
Just maybe he's...!

11:02.620 --> 11:04.950
﻿Do you know which excavation site they're working at?

11:04.950 --> 11:07.240
﻿Ah, well, that's...

11:07.410 --> 11:08.910
﻿Oh, please wait one moment.

11:12.330 --> 11:15.210
﻿He said he'd take you there since he has something to deliver there it seems.

11:16.840 --> 11:18.010
﻿Really?!

11:41.860 --> 11:45.950
﻿Professor Harrison, I will surely solve the riddle of this ruin!

11:46.950 --> 11:50.200
﻿But I wonder just what kind of person is sleeping inside here?

11:50.870 --> 11:54.580
﻿Could it be some Pharaoh who once ruled over this land? Or maybe their queen?

11:54.580 --> 11:55.830
﻿Perhaps a prince?

11:55.840 --> 11:58.050
﻿Or even a beautiful princes—

12:00.340 --> 12:01.920
﻿Christian!

12:07.810 --> 12:10.020
﻿A beautiful princess...?

12:11.680 --> 12:13.350
﻿It really is you!

12:13.350 --> 12:15.020
﻿N-Nadja!

12:18.480 --> 12:19.780
﻿To think that I'd run into you again...

12:19.780 --> 12:22.190
﻿B-But, why are you here?

12:22.240 --> 12:26.370
﻿I'm looking for a person called Professor Edward Harrison.

12:26.370 --> 12:29.950
﻿Huh? How do you know the name of Professor Harrison?

12:29.950 --> 12:32.120
﻿You know him?!

12:32.120 --> 12:34.790
﻿Then he really is here, isn't he? Please let me see him!

12:34.790 --> 12:36.960
﻿He knows my Mother!

12:37.500 --> 12:43.630
﻿No, umm... this is difficult to say, but... the professor passed away a few years ago.

13:10.450 --> 13:15.540
﻿I see...
for you to have been Professor Harrison's apprentice...

13:16.020 --> 13:16.690
Yes.

13:17.420 --> 13:22.380
﻿But, for you to have come all this way to Egypt looking for him, and...

13:22.380 --> 13:24.380
﻿I don't know what to say.

13:24.380 --> 13:27.010
﻿No, it's all right.

13:27.050 --> 13:32.100
﻿For the Mummy Professor to suddenly come but of those ruins! This is just too convenient!

13:32.100 --> 13:37.230
﻿When my Mother was about the same age as me, she also came to Egypt

13:37.230 --> 13:40.980
﻿and apparently three years after meeting him, she danced with him.

13:40.980 --> 13:44.070
﻿I had no idea that Professor Harrison, who I looked up to as a father,

13:44.070 --> 13:47.650
﻿met with your mother like that in the past!

13:48.700 --> 13:52.120
﻿We've really been connected to each other since long ago, haven't we!

13:59.170 --> 14:01.920
﻿Hey, Christian... do you remember?

14:01.920 --> 14:04.760
﻿The brooch you helped me look for in Rome.

14:09.140 --> 14:13.350
﻿Ah, right... you said this was also a clue to help finding your mother, didn't you?

14:14.350 --> 14:17.560
﻿Look at this. There's, a ring inside of it.

14:21.940 --> 14:24.400
﻿Wait one second... this ring...

14:26.070 --> 14:27.820
﻿I know! I'm pretty sure it was...

14:27.820 --> 14:28.820
﻿What's the matter?

14:30.910 --> 14:35.620
﻿When the Professor first discovered this ruin, it was amongst the grave goods.

14:35.620 --> 14:39.830
﻿Basically, that's what we call the loot of treasure that's buried with someone in their tomb.

14:40.670 --> 14:43.880
﻿Anyway, most of it had been stolen by some grave robbers...

14:45.420 --> 14:49.300
﻿...but there was still a single ring that hall been left behind!

14:51.590 --> 14:53.220
﻿Take a look at this.

14:54.180 --> 14:54.760
﻿Here it is.

14:57.640 --> 15:00.230
﻿There's no stone set into this ring, but it looks exactly like yours, doesn't it?

15:01.850 --> 15:02.810
﻿You're right...

15:03.270 --> 15:06.020
﻿A stone could easily be inlaid into it later.

15:06.030 --> 15:06.780
Yeah.

15:06.780 --> 15:12.660
﻿And also, I remember hearing a story of the professor sending this ring to some noble,

15:12.660 --> 15:13.990
﻿who came to sightsee in Egypt.

15:13.990 --> 15:20.160
﻿Could it be that maybe your mother was related to that noble in some way?

15:24.790 --> 15:25.840
﻿Huh?

15:41.020 --> 15:43.310
﻿Th-This... moves!

15:48.230 --> 15:49.940
﻿W-What is that?

15:50.360 --> 15:51.780
﻿A swan?

15:54.620 --> 15:58.660
﻿This design! I remember seeing it somewhere before...

15:59.830 --> 16:01.120
I'm ﻿pretty sure it was in here..

16:02.040 --> 16:04.920
﻿Umm... umm... ah!

16:06.380 --> 16:07.130
﻿This is it!

16:07.130 --> 16:08.670
﻿Ah! Look at this!

16:08.670 --> 16:10.380
﻿Now that I look at it, it does look similar...

16:11.050 --> 16:17.430
﻿All of the symbols in here are the coats of arms of nobles who helped fund his excavation research!

16:17.430 --> 16:22.560
﻿And this one is... the crest of the Ducal House of Preminger of Vienna!

16:22.560 --> 16:24.690
﻿The crest of a Ducal House?

16:24.690 --> 16:25.520
﻿Yes.

16:25.520 --> 16:29.730
﻿Normally, the crests of nobles arc basically formed through marriage

16:29.730 --> 16:33.200
﻿depending on the two parties and slightly change over time.

16:33.990 --> 16:36.740
﻿Judging from this...

16:36.740 --> 16:42.000
﻿Your Mother might very well be related to the Ducal House of Preminger in Vienna!

16:42.870 --> 16:44.750
﻿The Ducal House of Preminger...

16:44.750 --> 16:46.960
﻿Then that means my Mother is in Vienna?

16:46.960 --> 16:52.670
﻿Ah! That much I can't conclude, but it'd be a good idea to confirm it there.

16:52.670 --> 16:57.220
﻿To learn all of these things all at once like this...!

16:57.220 --> 17:01.100
﻿I just feel as if my Mother's really close right now!

17:04.060 --> 17:06.440
﻿Christian! Thank you!!

17:08.060 --> 17:09.810
﻿This is all thanks to you!

17:12.280 --> 17:14.650
﻿Na... Na... Na..

17:19.450 --> 17:20.580
﻿Kennosuke!

17:25.540 --> 17:28.630
﻿Kennosuke!

17:28.630 --> 17:30.250
﻿Where are you?

17:31.090 --> 17:32.800
﻿Kennosuke!

17:33.710 --> 17:35.590
﻿Let me out of here!

17:35.590 --> 17:37.800
﻿It's dark and cramped inside here!

17:37.800 --> 17:39.800
﻿Kennosuke! Where are you?

17:40.390 --> 17:43.520
﻿Hurry and get me out of here before I turn into a mummy myself!

17:43.520 --> 17:45.930
﻿Where? Where are you?

17:45.940 --> 17:47.480
﻿In here!

17:49.940 --> 17:52.320
﻿You couldn't be... behind this wall?!

17:55.700 --> 17:56.650
﻿How?!

17:57.280 --> 18:00.070
﻿Kennosuke! Are you all right?

18:00.070 --> 18:02.580
﻿We're coming to help you right now!

18:09.880 --> 18:11.170
﻿Th-This is...!

18:11.170 --> 18:13.090
﻿What's going on?

18:14.090 --> 18:15.010
﻿Nadja!

18:16.880 --> 18:18.760
﻿Nadja! Are you all right?

18:18.760 --> 18:20.680
﻿Kennosuke, wait one second.

18:21.350 --> 18:23.010
﻿Let's try pushing this part of the wall together.

18:23.970 --> 18:25.020
﻿O-Okay!

18:25.020 --> 18:27.270
﻿Heave ho!

18:29.980 --> 18:31.350
﻿That surprised me!

18:31.360 --> 18:33.190
﻿For the wall to turn inside like that!

18:33.820 --> 18:35.480
﻿Nadja, did you get hurt?

18:35.480 --> 18:36.650
﻿No.

18:38.030 --> 18:39.610
﻿What? What's wrong?

18:40.660 --> 18:42.530
﻿This is amazing! This is an amazing discovery!

18:42.530 --> 18:43.700
﻿What is this?

18:43.700 --> 18:45.580
﻿For there to have been a trick like this!

18:46.500 --> 18:49.000
﻿We may able to prove what Professor Harrison thought,

18:49.000 --> 18:51.330
﻿that these are the ruins of the burial ground of the slaves

18:51.330 --> 18:55.550
﻿who served the Kuwaku Royal Family and Queen Plita!

18:56.590 --> 18:59.880
﻿Thank you, Kennosuke! This is all thanks to you!

19:00.820 --> 19:02.370
L-L-Let go!

19:01.800 --> 19:02.390
﻿Thank you!

19:02.390 --> 19:05.100
﻿Why did it have to be me?! Let go of me!

19:04.740 --> 19:05.100
Thank you!

19:05.100 --> 19:07.140
Stop it already!

19:07.140 --> 19:08.560
﻿N-Nadja!

19:09.940 --> 19:12.020
﻿The Ducal House of Preminger in Vienna...

19:13.440 --> 19:15.980
﻿If I go to Vienna, I might learn something!

19:28.700 --> 19:33.790
﻿Hey! We've come to pick you up!

19:45.890 --> 19:50.350
﻿Grossing over the seas from far away, we, the Dandelion Troupe...

19:50.350 --> 19:54.600
﻿shall bring all of you excavators that nostalgic breeze of Europe!

19:54.610 --> 19:56.900
﻿We've been waiting for this

21:24.280 --> 21:26.820
﻿Well then, be careful in your travels, Nadja.

21:26.820 --> 21:28.160
﻿I will!

21:28.160 --> 21:30.280
﻿Christian. You do your best too, okay?

21:30.280 --> 21:31.450
﻿Yep.

21:31.450 --> 21:33.080
﻿Nadja, hurry!

21:33.080 --> 21:34.940
﻿I know.

21:34.940 --> 21:35.960
﻿Bye.

21:35.960 --> 21:38.920
﻿Yeah. Goodbye.

21:41.340 --> 21:44.760
﻿All right! Let's head back to Europe then!

21:58.900 --> 22:02.070
﻿I want to hurry and see you soon, Mother.

22:14.470 --> 22:17.720
Paris is sunnier than London

22:14.470 --> 22:17.720
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:17.840 --> 22:20.930
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:17.840 --> 22:20.930
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:21.350 --> 22:27.520
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:21.350 --> 22:27.520
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:28.480 --> 22:29.720
Indeed

22:28.480 --> 22:29.720
Kitto

22:32.480 --> 22:34.900
It's not use worrying about it

22:32.480 --> 22:34.900
